extends layout

block content
  .wrapper
    section
      .content#news
        h1 Introduction
        p This is the very early alpha version of Black Dust. A browser strategy game that I started developing as the product for my web-developer bachelors project.
        p The game runs on Node.js with the Express.js framework using Socket.io for client-server communication, and a MongoDB database. 
        p My basic vision for the game is of a gameworld that is constantly changing. The world is covered by a veil of “black dust” that is essentially a storm of tiny particles that are pieces of the world that was before. You discover the world by using tether, a resource that you extract from the earth. When you use spells that spend your tether, the area that you targeted is rejoined with reality. 
        p You will reveal your surroundings by using spells and as you reveal more land you will discover remnants of the old world that was broken into pieces. The further you explore the more dangerous and valuable your surroundings may become.
        p As you discover new areas you will be able to add tiles to your own territory by building structures. Any tiles that you have not built on, will eventually fade away if left alone.
        p There will always be other players somewhere around you that you can befriend or attack. Combat will be a kind of advanced version of the board game, battleship. You discover enemy units based on concealment and you can attack them, but it’s best to know what might be hidden because other units may escalate your attack. An attack can end up being more than you bargained for. Diplomacy could also be a valuable endeavor.
        p There is no perma-death but your buildings and base may be raided if you fail to fend off invaders.
        p You can extract resources from tiles and features to construct new buildings and increase your power and wealth.
        p When you login to the game, you are placed in a location on the map based on a number of factors. When you log out of the game, you will be taken out of the gameworld and your area will be reclaimed by the dust.
        p The goal of the game is to live and prosper with your friends and to defeat your enemies, while going through a unique storyline that will eventually restore permanence to the world.
        hr
        p The game currently features:
        p - A very basic user interface
        p - Hexagonal map with terrain tiles
        p - One unit type with abilities and spells
        p - Unit movement and a spell that reveals new tiles
        p - It's Multiplayer
        p You navigate the map by click-and-drag and zoom with the mousewheel.
        p There is not a lot to do, just yet. :)
        p //Martin
        hr
  .fade


    
